Selection Sort
1.	Take an array of size n.
2.	Start an outer loop from index 0 to n-2.
3.	Assume the current index i contains the minimum element.
4.	Set minIndex = i.
5.	Start an inner loop from i+1 to n-1.
6.	Compare array[j] with array[minIndex].
7.	If array[j] is smaller, update minIndex = j.
8.	After the inner loop finishes, swap array[i] with array[minIndex].
9.	Repeat for all indices.
10.	Key Idea: Select the minimum element and place it at the beginning.

Time Complexity: O(n²)
Space Complexity: O(1)
